Let me analyze each method for N+1 issues.

1. `orders()`: `Order::all()` then for each order accesses `$o->user->name` and `$o->items->count()`. This is an N+1 issue — should eager load `user` and `items`. Fix: `Order::with('user', 'items')->get()`.

2. `orderShow(Order $order)`: accesses `$order->user->name` and `$order->items->map(... $item->product->label)`. For a single order, the items relation load is 1 query, and each item's product is N queries. Also user is 1 query. This is N+1 on items' products. Fix: `$order->load('user', 'items.product')`.

3. `enterpriseOrder()`: same as orderShow — accesses items->product for each item. Fix: eager load `items.product`.

4. `products()`: `Product::all()` then each product accesses `$p->category->label`. N+1. Fix: `Product::with('category')->get()`.

5. `productsByCategory(Category $category)`: `Product::where('category_id', $category->id)->get()` — no relation access. No N+1.

6. `productReviews(Product $product)`: `$product->reviews->map(... $r->user->name)`. Reviews for one product is one query, then each review's user is N queries. N+1. Fix: `$product->reviews()->with('user')->get()->map(...)`. Or `$product->load('reviews.user')` then access `$product->reviews`.

7. `productsWithoutCategory()`: `Product::whereNull('category_id')->get()` — no relation access. No N+1.

8. `categoryProducts(Category $category)`: `$category->products->map(... $p->reviews->count())`. Products for one category is one query, then each product's reviews count is N queries. N+1. Fix: eager load reviews: `$category->products()->with('reviews')->get()->map(...)`. Or `$category->load('products.reviews')`.

9. `userOrders(User $user)`: `$user->orders->map(... $o->items->count())`. Orders for one user is one query, then each order's items is N queries. N+1. Fix: `$user->orders()->with('items')->get()->map(...)` or `$user->load('orders.items')`.

10. `recentReviews()`: `Review::latest()->take(20)->get()->map(... $r->product->label, $r->user->name)`. Each review's product and user are N queries. N+1. Fix: `Review::with('product', 'user')->latest()->take(20)->get()->map(...)`.

